config BR2_PACKAGE_MABUR
	bool "mabur"
	default n
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUSB
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DEVOURER
	help
	  RTP-free FPV video link, drone side. maburd drives the SigmaStar
	  MI encoder in-process, applies per-layer RS UEP FEC + SBI framing,
	  and injects over a Realtek 8812EU or 8812CU via the devourer userspace
	  driver, with adaptive-link (RCF/DISC) feedback, air-clock pacing
	  and MAX_RANGE failsafe. One daemon: the separate encoder process
	  was folded into maburd, which drives the SigmaStar MI encoder
	  in-process.

	  https://github.com/gilankpam/mabur

if BR2_PACKAGE_MABUR

choice
	prompt "Radio card"
	default BR2_PACKAGE_MABUR_RADIO_8812EU
	help
	  The one Realtek chip maburd's devourer is built for. Exactly one:
	  each chip carries its own firmware + PHY/halrf tables (stripped
	  maburd, 2026-09-26: 8822E 1.08 MB, 8822C 1.27 MB, both 1.70 MB)
	  and the board carries one card. maburd on the wrong card fails
	  at CreateRtlDevice ("unsupported chip"). The choice also sets
	  maburd's wide-TX IGI floor at build time: off on the 8812EU,
	  devourer's default (0x35) on the 8812CU, whose 40 MHz inject
	  stalls on a silent channel without it.

config BR2_PACKAGE_MABUR_RADIO_8812EU
	bool "RTL8812EU (devourer rtl8822e)"
	help
	  OpenIPC URLLC AIO, RunCam WiFiLink 2 and clones.

config BR2_PACKAGE_MABUR_RADIO_8812CU
	bool "RTL8812CU (devourer rtl8822c)"
	help
	  EMAX Wyvern Link Alpha.

endchoice

endif
